title: The Ruhr Is Not Alone
subtitle: The rest of Germany has gone back to work.
view-if: crisis_ruhr = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Ruhr Is Not Alone

Everywhere else the strike is over. If the Ruhr fights alone, it will be beaten alone. The Freikorps are coming by train from Berlin and Bavaria.

- @rail: Ask the railwaymen to stop the troop trains.
- @strike: Call Central Germany out again.
- @negotiate: Press the Ruhr leaders to negotiate while they are strong.

@rail
subtitle: Some trains will stop. The railwaymen will pay for it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.crisis_momentum += 6;
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.repression += 3;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

At Hamm and Soest, the signalmen walk out. The troop trains wait for a day in the sidings, and some of the volunteers go home.

@strike
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A second front in Halle and Saxony, if the workers follow.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.crisis_momentum += 5;
Q.militancy += 6;
Q.repression += 5;
Q.district_halle_loyalty += 5;
Q.worker_support -= 1;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

The Leuna works and the Mansfeld pits stop again. Elsewhere in Saxony the workers are tired and stay at work.

@negotiate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's answer: bargain now, before the guns decide.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids bargaining with the government.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.crisis_momentum -= 3;
Q.e20_negotiated = 1;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.uspd_relation += 4;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Our delegates in Hagen argue for a settlement: the Red Army can win terms now, and will win none once Watter attacks. The Essen council calls them defeatists.
